I recently finished a game of nethack, in which I finished with 10,000
hit points.  I used no wishes in getting to this figure, and I only had
a few cursed scrolls of genocide to use on nurses.  And yes, it took an
enormous amount of time, more time even than getting 2,000,000,000 points.

Hint, the secret involves poly-piling, so if you have moral qualms about
that, read no further, and I won't upset your stomach.

The secret is:

Spellbooks of healing.  It takes a great deal of time to get potions or
scrolls, but there is a way to manufacture spellbooks by the thousands.
If you know all the spoilers, that should be enough for you to figure it 
out.  The biggest problem with spellbooks is the need to find enough food
to keep you going as you cast the spell over and over, and making sure that
you don't run out of mana.  Most nethackers out there probably haven't had
the need to worry about the mana, but if you push the envelope in this 
fashion, it becomes a factor.  For this reason, potions of gain level
are much, much better than potions of extra healing.

By the way, as I said, it takes a LOT of time, and there really are very
few game situations that could require much more than 200-250 hit points,
if you have decent armor and weapons, so since it has been done once already,
there's no reason for anyone to waste that much time getting hit points.
Unless you could get 100,000; that would be very impressive. ;^)

Oh, by the way, if you don't want to think about it, here's the method.

Create lots of monsters.  The best way is by using bags of tricks, which,
unlike wands and scrolls of create monster are reusable.  Then turn them to
stone.  You can do this by wielding a cockatrice corpse, having your pet
cockatrice turn them to stone, or by killing monsters with spells, wands,
or thrown weapons directly after having turned something to stone with 
your cockatrice corpse.  Now you have a lot of statues which do NOT 
contain spellbooks.  You need to turn them into statues which DO contain
spellbooks, and break them apart.  Statues turn into statues or boulders
when polymorphed, and, depending on how deep in the dungeon you are, the
statues have a certain probablility of containing spellbooks.  The lower
you are in the dungeon, the greater your probability.  You now have 
thousands of spellbooks very few of which are spellbooks of extra healing.
You know what to do from here.

